WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.385
Your Turnly sales portal brings your prospect list, calling, purchase links, and follow-ups together.

00:00:07.385 --> 00:00:12.065
These are actual portal screens with fictional training records.

00:00:12.065 --> 00:00:13.381
Start on Overview.

00:00:13.381 --> 00:00:18.280
Check your open prospects, follow-ups due, and completed purchases.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.595
Completed purchases come from confirmed gift-card payments.

00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:27.055
Changing a lead's stage by hand does not create a paid order.

00:00:28.055 --> 00:00:29.540
Scroll to Your link.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.025
Your credited sales.

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:36.520
Copy link puts your personal gift-card checkout address on your clipboard.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.496
Use your own link so a completed purchase can be attributed to you.

00:00:41.496 --> 00:00:45.728
Email a contact and Text a contact open the sending form.

00:00:45.728 --> 00:00:48.625
This example link is for training only.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:52.040
In your account, use the real link shown here.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.316
Open Prospects in the left menu.

00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:59.512
Use the search box and filters to find the person you need.

00:00:59.512 --> 00:01:02.713
My leads limits the view to your assignments.

00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:06.837
Filter by stage when you want to work new prospects first.

00:01:06.837 --> 00:01:11.318
Review the name and contact details, then choose Work prospect.

00:01:11.318 --> 00:01:17.861
Start calling opens the lead-working flow; it does not automatically place a telephone call.

00:01:18.861 --> 00:01:25.326
The lead workspace puts contact details on the left and your conversation outcome on the right.

00:01:25.326 --> 00:01:28.525
Read the saved notes before contacting someone.

00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:33.084
Use Edit primary details to correct a name, email, or phone number.

00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:37.168
Open scripts and objections gives you conversation guidance.

00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:44.790
Ask about upcoming closings, current closing gifts, and whether their clients live within Turnly's service area.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.703
Click Call lead beside the phone number.

00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:51.615
The call panel opens at the lower right.

00:01:51.615 --> 00:01:57.659
Check that it names the correct prospect, then click Start call when you are ready.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:01.882
Allow microphone access in your browser and use a headset.

00:02:01.882 --> 00:02:06.979
Once connected, the panel provides mute, keypad, and hang-up controls.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:09.601
End the call before navigating away.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:12.878
Recent calls to this lead shows call results.

00:02:12.878 --> 00:02:17.829
If dialing is blocked by a budget limit, contact your administrator.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:21.523
Choose Email link in the lead workspace.

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:25.227
Confirm the selected contact and the destination email.

00:02:25.227 --> 00:02:30.009
The message includes your tracked checkout link and the contact's name.

00:02:30.009 --> 00:02:37.418
Check the consent box only after verifying that the recipient agreed to receive Turnly emails at that address.

00:02:37.418 --> 00:02:38.967
Then choose Send email.

00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:45.769
A provider acceptance means the sending service accepted the message; it does not guarantee delivery.

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:48.598
No message is being sent in this training.

00:02:49.598 --> 00:02:53.085
Text link uses the phone number saved on the lead.

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:58.523
If the person asks you to use another number, choose Send to different number.

00:02:58.523 --> 00:03:04.869
Enter that number, confirm consent for texts to that number, then scroll down to Send text.

00:03:04.869 --> 00:03:10.517
This override applies only to that message; it does not change the saved contact.

00:03:10.517 --> 00:03:14.212
Send to different email works the same way for email.

00:03:14.212 --> 00:03:17.978
Never use an alternate recipient to bypass an opt-out.

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:27.267
After the conversation, select the accurate Outcome or Stage, add a useful conversation note, and click Save conversation.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:33.926
Follow-up and Not interested move the lead out of the active pipeline and into the follow-up flow.

00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:36.711
The first reminder is due in thirty days.

00:03:36.711 --> 00:03:43.098
If the person says not to contact them again, select the red Do Not Contact checkbox and save.

00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:47.786
That permanently stops outreach and removes the lead from follow-ups.

00:03:48.786 --> 00:03:51.920
Open Follow-ups to see the age-based groups.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.912
Thirty-day means zero through thirty days.

00:03:54.912 --> 00:03:57.832
Sixty-day means thirty-one through sixty.

00:03:57.832 --> 00:04:00.824
Ninety-day means sixty-one through ninety.

00:04:00.824 --> 00:04:03.673
Long term means ninety-one days or more.

00:04:03.673 --> 00:04:06.450
Click a group's count to see its leads.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.724
Age starts when the lead enters Follow-up or Not interested.

00:04:10.724 --> 00:04:16.493
Editing notes or switching between those two outcomes does not restart the clock.

00:04:16.493 --> 00:04:20.980
Review prior notes and contact preferences before reaching out.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:26.966
Deal pipeline shows the active stages and the number of leads in each one.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.594
Click a stage count to work that group.

00:04:29.594 --> 00:04:36.332
Follow-up and Not interested leads are handled in Follow-ups, and Do Not Contact leads are excluded.

00:04:36.332 --> 00:04:46.371
Your daily routine is simple: review your assigned prospects, prepare, call, share your personal checkout link with permission, and save the outcome.

00:04:46.371 --> 00:04:51.289
Return to Team playbook whenever you need the training or sales guidance.
